summary: unicode.equal_caseless, starts_with_caseless and ends_with_caseless compare by full case folding, so Straße equals STRASSE, a prefix or suffix ends only where a scalar does, and an accent spelled apart differs; unicode.equal_canonical_caseless also equates canonical spellings, U+00C5, A with U+030A and U+212B, and orders U+0345 after its folding; the ASCII forms in core/text fold only A to Z
